    "note": "**v1 PROD GATE — candidate 02** (fix for candidate-01's squashed middle bar; props = your exact repro + `debugLayout: true`).\n\n**Diagnosis:** the m0 was symmetric, but the row bands were multi-unit split weights — the engine distributes the quantization remainder OUTSIDE-IN (edges first, center LAST), so ancestor ±px drift starved the CENTER row by 17px.\n\n**Fix (handbook rung 3/5):** one EQUAL split cell per bar (spread ≤1px at any canvas, guaranteed) + the gap carved by a constant `placement.inset` fraction on each bar tile. Verified equal ±1px across 1280×800 / 1001×733 / 1920×1080 / 640×400 / 607×401, both orientations.\n\n**Your geometry contract:** new `debugLayout` prop (on in this candidate, in the Animation-fold style) — bars are tagged `bar` and `withLayoutContract` asserts equal height (horizontal) / equal width (vertical), tol 2%; violation renders a LAYOUT_CONTRACT error mosaic. 20/20 unit tests incl. the repro locked; CLI e2e 4/4.\n\n**Look-shift to judge:** bars are ~7% thinner at the same gap (the gap now lives inside each row band, incl. a half-gap at the plot's top/bottom edges).",
